{"name":"Lost in Sadness","hex":"#151632","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of lose"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having wandered from, or unable to find, the way.","In an unknown location; unable to be found."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lost"},{"term":"sadness","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state or emotion of being sad.","An event in one's life that causes sadness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sadness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sadness","blocks":[{"text":"Sadness is an emotional pain associated with, or characterized by, feelings of disadvantage, loss, despair, grief, helplessness, disappointment and sorrow. An individual experiencing sadness may become quiet or lethargic, and withdraw themselves from others. An example of severe sadness is depression, a mood which can be brought on by major depressive disorder or persistent depressive disorder. Crying can be an indication of sadness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/S%C3%A9pulcre_Arc-en-Barrois_111008_12.jpg/330px-S%C3%A9pulcre_Arc-en-Barrois_111008_12.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sadness","wikidata":"Q169251"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Paolo_Monti_-_Serie_fotografica_%28Venezia%2C_1953%29_-_BEIC_6363533.jpg/500px-Paolo_Monti_-_Serie_fotografica_%28Venezia%2C_1953%29_-_BEIC_6363533.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Paolo_Monti_-_Serie_fotografica_%28Venezia%2C_1953%29_-_BEIC_6363533.jpg/500px-Paolo_Monti_-_Serie_fotografica_%28Venezia%2C_1953%29_-_BEIC_6363533.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sad girls. Photo by Paolo